ed_categories":"Bars, Nightlife, Restaurants","shared_category_count":3},{"business_id":"_C7QiQQc47AOEv4PE3Kong","name":"Commander's Palace","shared_categories":"Bars, Nightlife, Restaurants","shared_category_count":3},{"business_id":"JhpRI9m71ybWHkAqRdL0Tg","name":"The Avenue Pub","shared_categories":"Bars, Nightlife, Restaurants","shared_category_count":3},{"business_id":"_Bi9kN_eR75G1eqIl7S3pA","name":"The Bulldog","shared_categories":"Bars, Nightlife, Restaurants","shared_category_count":3},{"business_id":"AU-B663F3MPO7W-goWwwXA","name":"B Mac's","shared_categories":"Bars, Nightlife","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"TMBbCDQG6bENJoQSST0XiA","name":"Brigtsen's Restaurant","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"mhrW9O0O5hXGXGnEYBVoag","name":"Jacques-Imo's Cafe","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"8KnMSrMuTI2AtHZ2LOI8OQ","name":"Maurepas Foods","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"Zi-F-YvyVOK0k5QD7lrLOg","name":"Muriel's Jackson Square","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"pKykk7lnD6Tf9wSzJYRyJA","name":"Starbucks","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0}],"text":[{"business_id":"5HZPNcMR5dHQ1OyOb-RDgw","review_id":"eKTVF57tWgYK_Ob9QnZrxA","date":"2009-06-27T22:17:12","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9431312680244446,"text_excerpt":"So this is a nice, reasonably priced place in a lovely part of town. It's warm, inviting, and very comfortable. We showed up around 8 on Saturday and even though they were busy, we got a seat immediately and service was quick. Service was really top notch, and prices were very reasonable (2 main courses, a starter, bottle of wine and dessert for under $75.) The Italian house salad is surprisingly special because of the light vinaigrette and the pine nuts. They have daily specials; I tried the butternut squash ravioli. My partner had the spaghetti and meatballs and we shared an order of bruscetta. The food is good but not excellent. As it is, it is good food in a really lovely atmosphere a..."},{"business_id":"5HZPNcMR5dHQ1OyOb-RDgw","review_id":"mkUaqETYohnZ1xzFtyX27g","date":"2012-11-24T21:37:02","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9391449689865112,"text_excerpt":"The last two times I've been we had great pizza and decent pasta fare. The paninis are creative and tasty--love the prima with artichoke hearts and goat cheese. I also really like the side salads--mixed greens with pine nuts and balsamic--pretty good for a side. I've never been inside, but that is because the outdoor space is amazing. It is shady, has great views of Esplanade for people watching and is beautifully lit at night. It's a great casual neighborhood restaurant overall."},{"business_id":"5HZPNcMR5dHQ1OyOb-RDgw","review_id":"VbxAtoTFsSJDMyz-jSq1xg","date":"2020-11-22T21:27:29","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9374657869338989,"text_excerpt":"It's a shame that I live here in the neighborhood and had never been to Nonna Mia until last night. We enjoyed the weather and sat outside in their patio courtyard area. Disposable throwaway menus were given to us and our server wore a face shield (though without a mask... does that help anything?). The food though was really really great. The breadsticks were doughy and hot and delicious. Pass on the parm cheese sauce, it didn't really have much flavor. We also ordered the Quattro Formagio Pizza & Prima Calzone. The pizza was thin with a puffy and soft crust and was pretty good. The calzone was good sized and I loved the fillings, artichokes, cheese, onions. All the yummy things. Overall..."}],"visual":[{"business_id":"5HZPNcMR5dHQ1OyOb-RDgw","photo_id":"hAO1rW-UOQydBxZbHl7o2Q","label":"outside","image_url":"/photos/hAO1rW-UOQydBxZbHl7o2Q.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.9248543381690979},{"business_id":"5HZPNcMR5dHQ1OyOb-RDgw","photo_id":"Ea1uZ9wx5lK3NQKEfL8a5w","label":"food","image_url":"/photos/Ea